{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CfdtGNQjZWrzgcF9snGtx","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I submitted a mean-variance portfolio across all 423 signals, fitted only on the 1970–1999 training data, with the covariance matrix shrunk 90% toward its diagonal so the weights don't chase noise. Its training Sharpe is 2.87 but its validation Sharpe (2000–2012) is only 0.27, so most of what it found in training didn't carry forward.\n\nI used 4 of the 5000 backtests on purpose. Individual signal Sharpes barely repeat from one half of the training period to the other (correlation 0.14), and a search over thousands of validation runs would mostly fit noise in 2000–2012. That would push the reported validation number up without making the portfolio any better going forward. I picked the method that did best in walk-forward tests within the training data (about 0.58 out-of-sample there), then checked only four candidates on validation. Even that small check makes 0.27 a slightly optimistic estimate."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":446,"cache_read_input_tokens":10013,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":446},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"d981685b-914f-4615-a3f5-f60a80caa5ff","uuid":"01ad495b-a0ef-41cb-887f-a2f72e5d70e1","timestamp":"2026-10-02T18:29:09.632Z","request_id":"req_011CfdtGNAbDfMwNKDBXt74P"}
